-- EXPECT-ERROR: the precondition `_ > 0` of `g`
-- A named function passed as a fold's step, its ELEMENT parameter refined
-- (2026-10-18, review of the fold-accumulator invariants phase 1): `g`'s
-- `{Int | _ > 0}` return is proved assuming `x > 0`, but `ys` is an unrefined
-- list, so nothing says what `List.fold_left` hands `g` meets it.  The demand
-- was PROVED and `cap verified` accepted this module, although `go([0 - 5])`
-- is -5.  A skip naming the unmet precondition, an error under
-- `cap verified`.  Accept twin: accept/t388 (the same `g` over a refined list).
mod NamedStepElementPrecondition do
  cap verified
  fn need_pos(k : {Int | _ > 0}) : Int do k end
  fn g(_a : Int, x : {Int | _ > 0}) : {Int | _ > 0} do x end
  fn go(ys : List(Int)) : Int do need_pos(List.fold_left(ys, 1, g)) end
end
